```python
text = input("Enter string: ").lower()
vowels_list = 'aeiou'
counts = {'Vowels': 0, 'Consonants': 0}

for char in text:
    if char.isalpha():
        if char in vowels_list:
            counts['Vowels'] += 1
        else:
            counts['Consonants'] += 1

print("Final Character Count:", counts)
```
This execution block ensures non-alphabet characters are safely bypassed while strictly categorizing vowels and consonants into a tracked dictionary matrix.
